Subregion name: grassland_overworld
Subregion description: Sunny grassland overworld opening stretch: rolling green hills, scattered bushes, a starting pipe, floating brick and question-mark item blocks, coins, the first low gaps, and patrolling shell-and-mushroom enemies teaching the core jumping rhythm at the level's left edge.
Subregion plan: This region is the opening left-to-right stretch of the platformer, occupying the leftmost 35 m of the stage and reading as a single continuous grassland course. It sits directly in front of the sunny grassland backdrop panel that forms its rear wall; all terrain and gameplay elements stand forward of that panel within the depth band, concentrated on a shallow lateral playing plane (roughly the front 2-4 m of the available depth) so the stretch reads cleanly as a side-scrolling course rather than a deep diorama. The dominant structure is a continuous ground plane running the full width along the bottom, built from chunky cube-like terrain blocks, with low rolling green hill mounds rising gently above it and a few scattered low bushes resting on the surface. This is the gentlest part of the level's difficulty curve, so the ground stays mostly level and unbroken with only one or two narrow low gaps toward the right portion of the stretch, where the floor drops out briefly and resumes — short enough to clear with a basic jump and teaching the core jumping rhythm before the harder zones to the right. The far-left edge holds the level's entry point: a short green warp pipe standing on the ground where the hero's journey begins, with the immediate area around it kept open and obstacle-free as a safe starting area. Above the ground, at roughly jump-reachable height, a sparse layer of suspended item blocks (brick blocks and question-mark blocks) floats in small clusters and short rows, positioned over and just before the gaps and key jump points; coins are arranged in arcs and short horizontal rows that trace the intended leap paths, curving over the gaps and rising toward the floating blocks to guide movement rightward. A small number of simple rounded patrolling enemies move back and forth along the ground surface in the open mid-section, spaced so they introduce timing and avoidance gradually. The whole stretch slopes its layout so it begins flat and calm at the left starting pipe and grows slightly more demanding toward the right boundary, where the ground and platform logic flow continuously into the next segment of the level. Vertical space above the floating block layer stays mostly open sky, leaving the upper portion of the bounding box clear.



