        Plan for this region: This region is the underground cavern stretch of the platformer, occupying the full 25 m width between the grassland overworld on its left and the airborne challenge on its right, and reading as one continuous left-to-right course set inside an enclosed rock chamber. It stands forward of the dark cavern backdrop panel that forms its rear wall, with all terrain and gameplay elements concentrated on a shallow lateral playing plane (roughly the front 2-4 m of the available depth) so the stretch reads as a side-scrolling course rather than a deep diorama. The defining trait versus the open grassland is vertical compression: a thick band of chunky cube-like stone fills the upper portion of the bounding box as a rough cavern ceiling, lowering the usable play column into the bottom third to two-fifths of the height and giving the segment a cramped, boxed-in feel. The floor is a discontinuous strip of cube-like terrain blocks (stone-grey rock rather than grassy green) interrupted by several pits where the floor drops out entirely down to the bottom of the chamber, requiring jumps to cross; these pits are the central hazard and are more frequent and demanding than the grassland's single gentle gap, matching the rising difficulty curve. Between floor and ceiling, stacked brick-block platforms and short narrow ledges sit at staggered heights, forming a tighter vertical climb-and-drop path that the hero hops between to traverse pits and reach coin clusters tucked into pockets and along ledge edges. Coins are arranged in tight clusters and short rows that trace the intended jump arcs over the pits and up onto the raised platforms. A small number of simple rounded crawling enemies patrol along the lower floor segments and ledges, spaced to demand timing without overwhelming. The left edge holds the entry point where the hero arrives from the grassland's downward warp pipe — a green warp pipe positioned so the player emerges here into the cavern, with