        Plan for this region: This region is the airborne middle stretch of the platformer, occupying the 30 m width between the underground cavern on its left and the castle stronghold on its right, and reading as one continuous left-to-right course suspended high in open sky. It stands forward of the high-altitude sky backdrop panel that forms its rear wall, with all platforms, hazards, and gameplay elements concentrated on a shallow lateral playing plane (roughly the front 2-4 m of the available depth) so the stretch reads as a side-scrolling course rather than a deep diorama. The defining trait of this segment, in contrast to the grounded grassland and the enclosed cavern, is the absence of a continuous floor: the lower portion of the bounding box is left empty as a deep open drop, so the hero must cross the entire width by leaping between discrete suspended platforms with nothing solid beneath them. The left edge holds a small stable arrival platform positioned so the hero emerges here from the cavern's upward exit pipe, giving a brief safe footing before the gap begins; from there the traversal path is a staggered chain of floating platforms (a mix of soft rounded cloud platforms and chunky cube-like brick platforms) set at varying heights across the width, spaced at jump-reachable intervals so the route rises and falls as it advances rightward. Across the widest, deepest portions of the gap where fixed platforms cannot bridge the distance, moving lift platforms travel along short repeating paths (vertically or horizontally) to ferry the hero across, demanding timed jumps. Simple spinning or hopping obstacles are positioned along the platform path as avoidable hazards that punish imprecise leaps. A checkpoint marker stands on one of the more stable mid-stretch platforms roughly midway across, marking the progress waypoint. Set apart from the main route, a hidden bonus alcove sits tucked at an out-of-the-way height (high above the main path or below an overhang of platforms), reachable only by a precise optional jump and holding a cluster of rewards. Coins are arranged in arcs and short rows that trace the intended leap trajectories, curving between platforms and over the deepest gaps to guide movement rightward and hint at the bonus route. This is among the harder stretches of the level, so platform spacing and hazard density increase from the calmer left entry toward the right, where the platform path delivers the hero to the right boundary and the layout flows continuously into the castle stronghold segment. The vertical space well below the platform chain stays clear as the open drop, and the upper portion of the box stays mostly open sky apart from the highest platforms and the bonus alcove.
